# --- Stage 0 contract of record (BF-1) -------------------------------------
# The Stage 0 governing RFC is a CONTRACT, not an ephemeral review document: a
# third party must be able to recover it after `git clone`. This negates ONLY
# that one file; every other review/audit/RFC/acceptance rule above is left
# intact. (Last matching rule wins, so this must stay at the end of the file.)
!docs/STAGE0_PARAMETERIZED_GAIT_RFC_REV1.md

# --- Stage 0 corpus commit scope (owner decision, 2026-10-06) ---------------
# Commit the reconstruction chain (theta list, per-episode records/metrics/
# provenance/integrity/manifest/run_config) and the corpus index. Exclude the
# bulky, regenerable raw streams and canonical sample dumps (~510 MB -> a few
# MB). Raw traces and samples.jsonl are regenerable from the committed theta
# list + tools/run_stage0_dataset.py. See
# docs/STAGE0_CLOSURE_COMPLETION_REPORT.md.
dataset/stage0/**/trace/
dataset/stage0/**/dataset/samples.jsonl

# Superseded pre-declaration ring0 episodes, moved aside (not part of the
# pre-registered corpus, preserved for traceability, not committed).
dataset/_superseded_predeclaration/

# --- Stage 1 contract of record (BF-1 prevention) ---------------------------
# Same rationale as the Stage 0 negation above: the Stage 1 Dynamics Dataset
# RFC is a pre-implementation CONTRACT, not an ephemeral review document, and
# must be recoverable after `git clone`. This negates ONLY that one file; the
# broad RFC ignore rule above stays intact for everything else.
# (Last matching rule wins, so this must stay at the end of the file.)
!docs/STAGE1_DYNAMICS_DATASET_RFC.md
